            <ArticleTitle>Non-Hodgkin's lymphoma disguised as odontogenic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>99-100</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient was treated for infraorbital swelling, nonvital teeth and a periapical lesion. Suspected malignancy, confirmed with an early biopsy, resulted in diagnosis of non-Hodgkin's lymphoma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
